 "news": {
  "date": "2026-09-28",
  "asof": "2026-09-30 10:54 UTC",
  "headline": "Gold fell three and a half percent into a war escalation \u2014 and that is the whole story of this market",
  "standfirst": "Trump rejected Tehran\u2019s proposal on Saturday \u2014 terms that asked the US to release frozen Iranian funds, lift sanctions and end its naval blockade in exchange for reopening the Strait of Hormuz within seven days \u2014 and Iran said it would not soften its demands. WTI rose 4.22% to $96.31 and Brent 4.02% to $108.50, undoing half of last week\u2019s 7.8% decline in one session. And yet the largest move on the board was gold, down 3.52% to $4,184.50 \u2014 a 2.41 sigma fall, into an escalation, because the ten-year is at 5.2%, a 19-year high, and the five-year is holding above five. Equities fell broadly with 65% of issues lower: S&P \u22120.77%, Nasdaq \u22120.92%. In the book OKTA rose 3.58% to 202.18, taking back almost all of Friday\u2019s sector downgrade and returning to +0.97R, while GOOG and AAPL drifted lower with the tape. Heat 3.05R against 3.0R, unchanged for a thirteenth session.",
